      "heading": null,
      "bodyHtml": "<p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Companies with large fleets inevitably face fuel management issues. And for good reason: fuel costs often account for a significant portion of a fleet’s total expenses. In this case, a fuel monitoring system is the ultimate solution for optimizing expense accounting.</span></p><p class=\"font_7 wixui-rich-text__text\"><span class=\"wixui-rich-text__text\">Fuel management system is based on data available from on-board computer or aftermarket fuel level sensors installed in a vehicle’s fuel tank. Data transmitted to the tracking system allows detecting fuel theft or excessive fuel consumption, which helps to find ways to save 15% or more on fuel costs and increase fleet efficiency by 30% or more. According to statistics, Jaxicloud Fleet Management fleet management system implementation for fuel control pays for itself within 3-4 months.</span></p>",
      "bodyText": "Companies with large fleets inevitably face fuel management issues. And for good reason: fuel costs often account for a significant portion of a fleet’s total expenses. In this case, a fuel monitoring system is the ultimate solution for optimizing expense accounting.Fuel management system is based on data available from on-board computer or aftermarket fuel level sensors installed in a vehicle’s fuel tank. Data transmitted to the tracking system allows detecting fuel theft or excessive fuel consumption, which helps to find ways to save 15% or more on fuel costs and increase fleet efficiency by 30% or more. According to statistics, Jaxicloud Fleet Management fleet management system implementation for fuel control pays for itself within 3-4 months.",
